tpad (7.0.0.6-1) stonking; urgency=high

  * Restore builds with GCC's implicit-function-declaration error enabled.
  * Replace obsolete Ubuntu build dependencies and support split systemd.
  * Replace removed CDBS autotools rules with the debhelper sequencer.
  * Remove generated build state containing developer-specific paths.
  * Prevent shell injection when opening files in another tpad window.
  * Fix out-of-bounds hash and BOM reads and hash complete binary files.
  * Save files atomically and repair open-guard backup handling.
  * Fix find-and-replace overflow, Base64, word-count, and startup bugs.
  * Restore detached zero-, single-, and multi-file launcher behavior.
  * Preserve external-change checks when Save As targets the open file.
  * Fix GTK 3 callback signatures, font selection, spelling, and undo bugs.
  * Refresh generated Autotools files and make distcheck pass again.

